Z||000000||turbo86se||04-24-2000||12:29 PM||||<BR>hey guys, I'm writing a paper for extra credit for two of my classes, and I need several examples of how someone was scammed, or decieved by someone else. If anyone can help that would be greatly appreciated!!!  All I need is how it happened, how it was executed (step by step),  what happened after the suspect was caught, and what social skills allowed him/her to decieve the victim?<P>Please email me your story, turbo86se@webtv.net<BR>thanks again, and I really appreciate it! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||04-24-2000||08:03 PM||||One day I... I mean this guy I know was really hungry and noticed a baby with some candy. The suspect sized up the situation and made my... I mean his move. As the individual approached the toddler, he reached for the candy. Just then the cops came blazing around the corner firing bullets at the suspect. The suspect grabbed the child to use as a shield and managed to climb a fire escape to freedom. The suspect is still at large and I never intend to get caught, but the alleged suspect promises to never do it again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-24-2000||08:11 PM||||DAMN YOU, that was MY candy!||||reg||8
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||04-24-2000||08:55 PM||||I've been ripped off by a few clients in the past (one owed me a couple thousand dollars.. never paid.. but I didn't do anything about it.) but never scammed really.<P>what about girls, do they count? eg. talking with a girl you know all night.. things are really going good, getting along great.. then you ask her out and she says no. ok, that's not even close to a scam, it's just.. I dunno.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>(sorry for rambling.. I didn't get much sleep last night.......)||||reg||1
