Z||000005||Boodoggin||04-24-2000||10:37 PM||||Turbo 86SE, If you still need a story to write about maybe I can help you out, here it is... About a month ago in my home town of Boise the cops uncovered a massive pyramid scheme that hundreds of people in our area were involved in. This was no ordinary pyramid scheme it was really high stakes.  It was a really big deal here. It was the top story on the news for a coouple weeks A lot of people lost big $$, and a lot of people went to jail I think. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||04-25-2000||09:45 PM||||Here's a scam that was pulled on my sister... really sucked, don't do it, bad karma.  That said, here's how it went. My sister (the mark) was working at an all-night service station when a guy comes up to her asking for change for the payphone. He goes to use the phone. She gets a call from someone asking if anyone found a ring at the payphone. While she is on the phone the guy comes back.."look what I found.." The caller is distraught, Me-maws ring, only heirloom she has etc, and offers a $500 reward to the guy who found it.  Well, the guy is in a big hurry and can't hang out, but is willing to split the reward with my sis. Just give me $250 and get the five big when the (con) gets there. <BR>Well, y'all know that she had a loooong night waiting for the five hun to show up, not to mention the 'splaining she had to give her boss why she took $250 out of the till.  <P>Again, please do not pull this crap on anyone.  This is extremely bad Karma. Then again, you can only con a greedy person.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||BENGAL4||04-26-2000||11:14 AM||||Joel,<P>A few years ago, me and a friend went out to lunch during Christmas week. A guy came up to us in the parking lot and asked us for gas money. He said his car was on I-75 and he was trying to get home to Cleveland. I gave him 3 dollars and my friend gave him 2. <P>We sat in the car for a few minutes and I looked up and watched him walk into a market and come out with a small paper sack. We had been scammed. I started thinking and I realized that that Cleveland is on I-71 not I-75. My friend and I got a good chuckle out of it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by BENGAL4 (edited 04-27-2000).]||||reg||10
